/-!
# Gaussian laws as exponential families

The real Gaussian laws form an exponential family in two ways: with a fixed variance, with the
mean as parameter, and with a fixed mean, with the variance as parameter.

**Fixed variance.** The real Gaussian laws `𝒩(μ, v)` with a fixed variance `v` form the natural
exponential family (`T = id`) generated by any of them. Tilting `𝒩(m, v)` by `x ↦ η x` shifts its
mean by `v η`: the member of natural parameter `η` of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` is
`𝒩(m + v η, v)`. The log-partition function is the cumulant generating function
`ψ(η) = m η + v η² / 2` of `𝒩(m, v)`, so the mean map is `ψ'(η) = m + v η`. For `v ≠ 0` it takes
every real value: the means of the family are all of `ℝ`, the natural parameter of the mean `μ` is
`(μ - m) / v`, the member of mean `μ` is `𝒩(μ, v)`, and the divergence of the family in the mean
parametrization is `d(μ, μ') = (μ - μ')² / (2 v)`. Its extension `dbar` to every level is the same
expression, and the upper confidence level of KL-UCB is the Hoeffding-type level
`U(x, c) = x + √(2 v c)` of asymptotically optimal UCB (T. Lattimore and Cs. Szepesvári,
*Bandit Algorithms*, Cambridge University Press, 2020, Algorithm 6).
The variance function `ψ'' = v` is constant, so the Jeffreys prior is `√v` times Lebesgue
measure. For `v ≠ 0`, the posterior of the natural parameter after `s ≠ 0` observations of sum
`S` is the Gaussian law `𝒩((S - s m) / (s v), 1 / (s v))`, whose image by the mean map is
`𝒩(S / s, v / s)`: Thompson sampling with the Jeffreys prior samples the mean of an arm from
`𝒩(μ̂, v / s)`.

Gaussian arms with a known variance are the reference model of bandit identification: with
`d(μ, μ') = (μ - μ')² / (2 v)`, the transportation costs, the characteristic time and the
generalized likelihood ratio statistics of the exponential-family theory have closed forms, as in
A. Garivier and E. Kaufmann, *Optimal best arm identification with fixed confidence*, COLT 2016,
Section 2.2.

**Fixed mean.** The real Gaussian laws `𝒩(m, μ)` with a fixed mean `m` and variance `μ > 0` form
the exponential family generated by any of them, `𝒩(m, v)` with `v ≠ 0`, with the statistic
`T x = (x - m) ^ 2`. Tilting `𝒩(m, v)` by `x ↦ η (x - m) ^ 2` for `2 v η < 1` rescales its
variance: the member of natural parameter `η` is `𝒩(m, v / (1 - 2 v η))`. The natural parameters
are the `η < (2 v)⁻¹`, the log-partition function is `ψ(η) = -log (1 - 2 v η) / 2`, and the mean
map, the mean of `(X - m) ^ 2` under the member of natural parameter `η`, is its variance
`ψ'(η) = v / (1 - 2 v η)`. It takes every positive value: the means of the family are the
variances `(0, ∞)`, the natural parameter of the variance `μ` is `(v⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2`, the member of
mean `μ` is `𝒩(m, μ)`, and the divergence of the family in the mean parametrization is
`d(μ, μ') = (μ / μ' - 1 - log (μ / μ')) / 2`, the relative entropy between `𝒩(m, μ)` and
`𝒩(m, μ')` (`LMLExplore.klDiv_gaussianReal_gaussianReal`). For `v = 1` the natural parameter of
the variance `μ` is `(1 - μ⁻¹) / 2`. The law of the statistic `(X - m) ^ 2` under `𝒩(m, 1)` is the
gamma law of shape and rate `1 / 2`, so by the invariance of the mean parametrization under a change
of base member and under passing to the law of the statistic, `d` is the divergence of the gamma
laws of shape `1 / 2`. This is the model of Gaussian arms with a known mean and an
unknown variance, in which identification tasks ask questions about the variances of the arms.

## Main statements

Fixed variance, statistic `id`:

* `LMLExplore.expFamily_gaussianReal`: the member of natural parameter `η` of the exponential
  family of `𝒩(m, v)` is `𝒩(m + v η, v)`.
* `LMLExplore.deriv_cgf_gaussianReal`, `LMLExplore.deriv_cgf_gaussianReal_eq`: the mean map of the
  family is `η ↦ m + v η`.
* `LMLExplore.not_ae_eq_const_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the identity is not almost everywhere
  constant under `𝒩(m, v)`, the nondegeneracy assumption of the mean parametrization.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal`, `LMLExplore.mem_expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal`,
  `LMLExplore.setOf_forall_mem_expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the means of the family
  are all of `ℝ`, and every vector is a vector of means of the families of variances `v i ≠ 0`.
* `LMLExplore.natParam_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the natural parameter of the mean `μ` is
  `(μ - m) / v`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamily_natParam_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the member of mean `μ` is `𝒩(μ, v)`.
* `LMLExplore.image_expFamily_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the members of the family are the
  Gaussian laws of variance `v`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyDiv_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the divergence of the family is
  `d(μ, μ') = (μ - μ')² / (2 v)`.
* `LMLExplore.tendsto_expFamilyDiv_gaussianReal_atBot`,
  `LMLExplore.tendsto_expFamilyDiv_gaussianReal_atTop`: for `v ≠ 0`, `d(μ, μ') → ∞` as `μ'`
  tends to `-∞` or `∞`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyRate_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the extended divergence is
  `dbar(x, μ) = (x - μ)² / (2 v)`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyUpper_gaussianReal`, `LMLExplore.expFamilyUpper_top_gaussianReal`: for
  `v ≠ 0`, the upper confidence level is `U(x, c) = x + √(2 v c)` for finite `c`, and
  `U(x, ∞) = ∞`. `LMLExplore.expFamilyUpper_ofReal_gaussianReal` is the finite case for a real
  budget `c ≥ 0`.
* `LMLExplore.iteratedDeriv_two_cgf_gaussianReal`, `LMLExplore.jeffreysPrior_gaussianReal`: the
  variance function of the family is the constant `v`, and its Jeffreys prior is `√v` times
  Lebesgue measure.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_volume`,
  `LMLExplore.expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_jeffreysPrior`: for `v ≠ 0` and `s ≠ 0`
  observations of sum `S`, the posterior of the natural parameter for the flat prior and for the
  Jeffreys prior is `𝒩((S - s m) / (s v), 1 / (s v))`.
* `LMLExplore.map_deriv_cgf_expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_jeffreysPrior`: the image of that
  posterior by the mean map `ψ'` is `𝒩(S / s, v / s)`.

Fixed mean, statistic `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2`:

* `LMLExplore.expFamily_sub_sq_gaussianReal`: for `2 v η < 1`, the member of natural parameter `η`
  of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` is `𝒩(m, v / (1 - 2 v η))`.
* `LMLExplore.deriv_cgf_sub_sq_gaussianReal`: the mean map of the family is
  `η ↦ v / (1 - 2 v η)` on `2 v η < 1`.
* `LMLExplore.not_ae_eq_const_sub_sq_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` is not almost
  everywhere constant under `𝒩(m, v)`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyMeans_sub_sq_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the means of the family are
  `(0, ∞)`.
* `LMLExplore.natParam_sub_sq_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the natural parameter of the mean
  `μ > 0` is `(v⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamily_natParam_sub_sq_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the member of mean `μ > 0` is
  `𝒩(m, μ)`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyDiv_sub_sq_gaussianReal`: for `v ≠ 0`, the divergence of the family is
  `d(μ, μ') = (μ / μ' - 1 - log (μ / μ')) / 2` for `μ, μ' > 0`, the shape-`1 / 2` case of the
  divergence of the gamma laws.
* `LMLExplore.tendsto_expFamilyDiv_sub_sq_gaussianReal_nhdsGT_zero`,
  `LMLExplore.tendsto_expFamilyDiv_sub_sq_gaussianReal_atTop`: for `v ≠ 0`, `d(μ, μ') → ∞` as `μ'`
  tends to either endpoint `0` or `∞` of the means.
-/
public section

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Real Set

open scoped ENNReal NNReal Topology

namespace LMLExplore

variable {m : ℝ} {v : ℝ≥0}

/-! ### Fixed variance: the statistic `id` -/

/-- Tilting a Gaussian law shifts its mean: the member of natural parameter `η` of the exponential
family of `𝒩(m, v)` with statistic `id` is `𝒩(m + v η, v)`. For `v = 0`, both sides are the Dirac
mass at `m`. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamily_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (v : ℝ≥0) (η : ℝ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamily id η = gaussianReal (m + v * η) v := by
  rw [Measure.expFamily_def]
  exact TauCeti.Probability.gaussianReal_tilted_mul m v η

/-- The mean map of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` is `η ↦ m + v η`. -/
@[simp]
theorem deriv_cgf_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (v : ℝ≥0) (η : ℝ) :
    deriv (cgf id (gaussianReal m v)) η = m + v * η := by
  -- The log-partition function is the cumulant generating function `η ↦ m η + v η² / 2`.
  rw [show cgf id (gaussianReal m v) = fun η ↦ m * η + v * η ^ 2 / 2 from
    funext fun η ↦ cgf_gaussianReal HasLaw.id η]
  have h : HasDerivAt (fun η ↦ m * η + v * η ^ 2 / 2) (m * 1 + v * (2 * η ^ 1 * 1) / 2) η :=
    ((hasDerivAt_id η).const_mul m).add ((((hasDerivAt_id η).pow 2).const_mul _).div_const 2)
  rw [h.deriv]
  ring

/-- The mean map of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` is the function `η ↦ m + v η`. -/
theorem deriv_cgf_gaussianReal_eq (m : ℝ) (v : ℝ≥0) :
    deriv (cgf id (gaussianReal m v)) = fun η ↦ m + v * η :=
  funext (deriv_cgf_gaussianReal m v)

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the identity is not almost everywhere constant under `𝒩(m, v)`: the Gaussian law
has no atoms. This is the nondegeneracy assumption of the mean parametrization of the exponential
family of `𝒩(m, v)`. -/
lemma not_ae_eq_const_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (c : ℝ) :
    ¬ id =ᵐ[gaussianReal m v] fun _ ↦ c := by
  have := nullSingletonClass_gaussianReal (μ := m) hv
  intro h
  obtain ⟨x, hx, hxc⟩ := (h.and (Measure.ae_ne _ c)).exists
  exact hxc hx

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the means of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` are all of `ℝ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyMeans id = univ := by
  have hv' : (v : ℝ) ≠ 0 := NNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hv
  refine eq_univ_of_forall fun μ ↦ ?_
  rw [Measure.mem_expFamilyMeans_iff, integrableExpSet_id_gaussianReal, interior_univ]
  exact ⟨(μ - m) / v, mem_univ _, by rw [deriv_cgf_gaussianReal]; field_simp; ring⟩

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, every real number is a mean of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)`. -/
lemma mem_expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (μ : ℝ) :
    μ ∈ (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyMeans id := by
  simp [hv]

/-- For variances `v i ≠ 0`, every vector is a vector of means of the exponential families of
the `𝒩(m, v i)`: `μ i` is a mean of the family of `𝒩(m, v i)` for every `i`. -/
lemma setOf_forall_mem_expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal {ι : Type*} (m : ℝ) {v : ι → ℝ≥0}
    (hv : ∀ i, v i ≠ 0) :
    {μ : ι → ℝ | ∀ i, μ i ∈ (gaussianReal m (v i)).expFamilyMeans id} = univ := by
  simp [hv]

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the natural parameter of the member of mean `μ` of the exponential family of
`𝒩(m, v)` is `(μ - m) / v`. -/
@[simp]
theorem natParam_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (μ : ℝ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).natParam id μ = (μ - m) / v := by
  have hv' : (v : ℝ) ≠ 0 := NNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hv
  have h := Measure.deriv_cgf_natParam (ρ := gaussianReal m v) (T := id) (μ := μ)
    (by simp [hv])
  rw [deriv_cgf_gaussianReal] at h
  field_simp
  linarith

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the member of mean `μ` of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` is `𝒩(μ, v)`. -/
theorem expFamily_natParam_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (μ : ℝ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamily id ((gaussianReal m v).natParam id μ) = gaussianReal μ v := by
  have hv' : (v : ℝ) ≠ 0 := NNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hv
  rw [expFamily_gaussianReal, natParam_gaussianReal m hv]
  congr 1
  field_simp
  ring

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the members of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` are the Gaussian laws
`𝒩(μ, v)` of variance `v`, for every mean `μ`. -/
theorem image_expFamily_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamily id '' interior (integrableExpSet id (gaussianReal m v)) =
      range fun μ ↦ gaussianReal μ v := by
  ext Q
  rw [Measure.mem_image_expFamily_iff (not_ae_eq_const_gaussianReal m hv),
    expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal m hv]
  simp only [mem_univ, true_and, expFamily_natParam_gaussianReal m hv, mem_range]

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the divergence of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` in the mean
parametrization is `d(μ, μ') = (μ - μ')² / (2 v)`, the relative entropy between `𝒩(μ, v)` and
`𝒩(μ', v)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamilyDiv_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (μ μ' : ℝ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyDiv id μ μ' = (μ - μ') ^ 2 / (2 * v) := by
  have hv' : (v : ℝ) ≠ 0 := NNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hv
  rw [Measure.expFamilyDiv_def, natParam_gaussianReal m hv, natParam_gaussianReal m hv,
    cgf_gaussianReal HasLaw.id, cgf_gaussianReal HasLaw.id]
  field_simp
  ring

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the divergence `d(μ, μ') = (μ - μ')² / (2 v)` of the exponential family of
`𝒩(m, v)` tends to infinity as `μ' → -∞`. -/
theorem tendsto_expFamilyDiv_gaussianReal_atBot (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (μ : ℝ) :
    Filter.Tendsto ((gaussianReal m v).expFamilyDiv id μ) Filter.atBot Filter.atTop := by
  have hv' : 0 < 2 * (v : ℝ) := by positivity
  rw [funext (expFamilyDiv_gaussianReal m hv μ)]
  have h : Filter.Tendsto (fun μ' : ℝ ↦ μ - μ') Filter.atBot Filter.atTop := by
    simpa only [sub_eq_add_neg] using
      Filter.tendsto_atTop_add_const_left _ μ Filter.tendsto_neg_atBot_atTop
  exact ((Filter.tendsto_pow_atTop two_ne_zero).comp h).atTop_div_const hv'

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the divergence `d(μ, μ') = (μ - μ')² / (2 v)` of the exponential family of
`𝒩(m, v)` tends to infinity as `μ' → ∞`. -/
theorem tendsto_expFamilyDiv_gaussianReal_atTop (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (μ : ℝ) :
    Filter.Tendsto ((gaussianReal m v).expFamilyDiv id μ) Filter.atTop Filter.atTop := by
  have hv' : 0 < 2 * (v : ℝ) := by positivity
  rw [funext (expFamilyDiv_gaussianReal m hv μ)]
  simp_rw [sub_sq_comm μ]
  have h : Filter.Tendsto (fun μ' : ℝ ↦ μ' - μ) Filter.atTop Filter.atTop := by
    simpa only [sub_eq_add_neg, id] using
      Filter.tendsto_atTop_add_const_right _ (-μ) Filter.tendsto_id
  exact ((Filter.tendsto_pow_atTop two_ne_zero).comp h).atTop_div_const hv'

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the extended divergence of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` is
`dbar(x, μ) = (x - μ)² / (2 v)` at every level `x`, since every level is a mean. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamilyRate_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (x μ : ℝ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyRate id x μ = ENNReal.ofReal ((x - μ) ^ 2 / (2 * v)) := by
  rw [Measure.expFamilyRate_eq_ofReal_expFamilyDiv (mem_expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal m hv x)
    (mem_expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal m hv μ), expFamilyDiv_gaussianReal m hv]

/-- For `v ≠ 0` and a finite budget `c`, the upper confidence level of the exponential family of
`𝒩(m, v)` is `U(x, c) = x + √(2 v c)`, the index of asymptotically optimal UCB. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamilyUpper_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (x : ℝ) (c : ℝ≥0) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyUpper id x c = ((x + √(2 * v * c) : ℝ) : EReal) := by
  have hv' : (0 : ℝ) < v := NNReal.coe_pos.2 (pos_iff_ne_zero.2 hv)
  have hx : x ≤ x + √(2 * v * c) := le_add_of_nonneg_right (sqrt_nonneg _)
  refine le_antisymm (Measure.expFamilyUpper_le_iff.2
    ⟨EReal.coe_le_coe_iff.2 hx, fun q _ hxq hqc ↦ EReal.coe_le_coe_iff.2 ?_⟩)
    (Measure.le_expFamilyUpper_of_expFamilyRate_le (mem_expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal m hv _) hx ?_)
  · -- `(x - q)² / (2 v) ≤ c` gives `q - x ≤ √(2 v c)`.
    rw [expFamilyRate_gaussianReal m hv, ← ENNReal.ofReal_coe_nnreal,
      ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal_iff c.coe_nonneg, div_le_iff₀ (by positivity)] at hqc
    have := le_sqrt_of_sq_le (show (q - x) ^ 2 ≤ 2 * v * c by nlinarith)
    linarith
  · rw [expFamilyRate_gaussianReal m hv, ← ENNReal.ofReal_coe_nnreal]
    refine ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal (le_of_eq ?_)
    rw [show (x - (x + √(2 * v * c))) ^ 2 = 2 * v * c by
      rw [sub_add_cancel_left, neg_sq, sq_sqrt (by positivity)]]
    field_simp

/-- For `v ≠ 0` and a real budget `c ≥ 0`, the upper confidence level of the exponential family of
`𝒩(m, v)` is `U(x, c) = x + √(2 v c)`. -/
theorem expFamilyUpper_ofReal_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (x : ℝ) {c : ℝ} (hc : 0 ≤ c) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyUpper id x (ENNReal.ofReal c) =
      ((x + √(2 * v * c) : ℝ) : EReal) := by
  rw [← Real.coe_toNNReal c hc, ENNReal.ofReal_coe_nnreal, expFamilyUpper_gaussianReal m hv]

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the upper confidence level of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` with an
infinite budget is `U(x, ∞) = ∞`: every mean `q ≥ x` is at finite extended divergence from `x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamilyUpper_top_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (x : ℝ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyUpper id x ⊤ = ⊤ := by
  refine (EReal.eq_top_iff_forall_lt _).2 fun y ↦
    (EReal.coe_lt_coe_iff.2 ((le_max_right x y).trans_lt (lt_add_one _))).trans_le ?_
  exact Measure.le_expFamilyUpper_of_expFamilyRate_le (mem_expFamilyMeans_gaussianReal m hv _)
    ((le_max_left x y).trans (le_add_of_nonneg_right zero_le_one)) le_top

/-- The variance function of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` is constant: the second
derivative of its log-partition function is `v` at every natural parameter. -/
@[simp]
theorem iteratedDeriv_two_cgf_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (v : ℝ≥0) (η : ℝ) :
    iteratedDeriv 2 (cgf id (gaussianReal m v)) η = v := by
  rw [iteratedDeriv_succ, iteratedDeriv_one, deriv_cgf_gaussianReal_eq]
  simp

/-- The Jeffreys prior of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` is `√v` times Lebesgue measure. -/
theorem jeffreysPrior_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (v : ℝ≥0) :
    (gaussianReal m v).jeffreysPrior id = ENNReal.ofReal √v • volume := by
  simp [Measure.jeffreysPrior_def, integrableExpSet_id_gaussianReal, withDensity_const]

/-- For `v ≠ 0` and `s ≠ 0` observations whose sum is `S`, the posterior of the natural parameter
of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` for the flat prior (Lebesgue measure) is the Gaussian law
`𝒩((S - s m) / (s v), 1 / (s v))`. -/
theorem expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_volume (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) {s : ℕ} (hs : s ≠ 0)
    (S : ℝ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyPosterior id volume s S =
      gaussianReal ((S - s * m) / (s * v)) (s * v)⁻¹ := by
  have hsv : (s : ℝ≥0) * v ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero (Nat.cast_ne_zero.2 hs) hv
  have ha : (0 : ℝ) < s * v := by positivity
  set μ₀ : ℝ := (S - s * m) / (s * v)
  -- the unnormalized posterior is a constant multiple `C` of `𝒩(μ₀, 1 / (s v))`, by completing the
  -- square `θ S - s (m θ + v θ² / 2) = s v μ₀² / 2 - s v (θ - μ₀)² / 2`
  set C : ℝ≥0∞ := ENNReal.ofReal (√(2 * π * (s * v : ℝ)⁻¹) * exp (s * v * μ₀ ^ 2 / 2))
  have hC0 : C ≠ 0 := by
    simp only [C, ne_eq, ENNReal.ofReal_eq_zero, not_le]
    positivity
  have hdens : (fun θ ↦ ENNReal.ofReal (exp (θ * S - s * cgf id (gaussianReal m v) θ))) =
      C • gaussianPDF μ₀ ((s : ℝ≥0) * v)⁻¹ := by
    ext θ
    have h2 : 0 < 2 * π * (s * v : ℝ)⁻¹ := by positivity
    rw [cgf_gaussianReal HasLaw.id, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, gaussianPDF, gaussianPDFReal,
      ← ENNReal.ofReal_mul (by positivity)]
    congr 1
    push_cast
    rw [mul_mul_mul_comm, mul_inv_cancel₀ (Real.sqrt_pos.2 h2).ne', one_mul, ← exp_add]
    congr 1
    simp only [μ₀]
    field_simp
    ring
  rw [Measure.expFamilyPosterior_def, integrableExpSet_id_gaussianReal, interior_univ, hdens,
    withDensity_smul' C _ ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top, ← gaussianReal_of_var_ne_zero _ (inv_ne_zero hsv),
    cond_smul _ _ hC0 ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top, cond_univ]

/-- For `v ≠ 0` and `s ≠ 0` observations whose sum is `S`, the posterior of the natural parameter
of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` for its Jeffreys prior is the Gaussian law
`𝒩((S - s m) / (s v), 1 / (s v))`: the Jeffreys prior is a constant multiple of the flat prior. -/
theorem expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_jeffreysPrior (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) {s : ℕ} (hs : s ≠ 0)
    (S : ℝ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyPosterior id ((gaussianReal m v).jeffreysPrior id) s S =
      gaussianReal ((S - s * m) / (s * v)) (s * v)⁻¹ := by
  have hv' : (0 : ℝ) < v := by positivity
  rw [jeffreysPrior_gaussianReal, Measure.expFamilyPosterior_smul
    (by simpa using Real.sqrt_pos.2 hv') ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top,
    expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_volume m hv hs]

/-- For `v ≠ 0` and `s ≠ 0` observations whose sum is `S`, the image of the posterior of the
natural parameter of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` for its Jeffreys prior by the mean map
`ψ'` is the Gaussian law `𝒩(S / s, v / s)`: the mean of a natural parameter drawn from the
posterior is distributed as `𝒩(μ̂, v / s)`, with `μ̂ = S / s` the empirical mean. -/
theorem map_deriv_cgf_expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_jeffreysPrior (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) {s : ℕ}
    (hs : s ≠ 0) (S : ℝ) :
    ((gaussianReal m v).expFamilyPosterior id ((gaussianReal m v).jeffreysPrior id) s S).map
        (deriv (cgf id (gaussianReal m v))) = gaussianReal (S / s) (v / s) := by
  have hv' : (v : ℝ) ≠ 0 := NNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hv
  have hs' : (s : ℝ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.2 hs
  rw [expFamilyPosterior_gaussianReal_jeffreysPrior m hv hs,
    deriv_cgf_gaussianReal_eq,
    show (fun η ↦ m + v * η) = (fun x ↦ x + m) ∘ (fun x ↦ (v : ℝ) * x) from
      funext fun η ↦ add_comm _ _,
    ← Measure.map_map (by fun_prop) (by fun_prop), gaussianReal_map_const_mul,
    gaussianReal_map_add_const]
  congr 1
  · field_simp
    ring
  · ext
    push_cast
    field_simp

/-! ### Fixed mean: the statistic `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` -/

section SubSq

variable {η μ μ' : ℝ}

/-- Tilting a Gaussian law by its squared deviation rescales its variance: for `2 v η < 1`, the
member of natural parameter `η` of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` with statistic
`x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` is `𝒩(m, v / (1 - 2 v η))`. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamily_sub_sq_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (v : ℝ≥0) (hη : 2 * v * η < 1) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamily (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) η =
      gaussianReal m (v / (1 - 2 * v * η)).toNNReal := by
  rw [Measure.expFamily_def]
  exact tilted_mul_sub_sq_gaussianReal m v hη

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the interior of the natural parameters of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)`
with statistic `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` is the open half-line `2 v η < 1`. -/
private lemma mem_interior_integrableExpSet_sub_sq_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) :
    η ∈ interior (integrableExpSet (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) (gaussianReal m v)) ↔
      2 * v * η < 1 := by
  rw [integrableExpSet_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv, interior_Iio,
    ← integrableExpSet_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv]
  -- Membership in `integrableExpSet` is integrability of the exponential, by definition.
  exact integrable_exp_mul_sub_sq_gaussianReal_iff m v η

/-- The mean map of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` with statistic `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` is
`η ↦ v / (1 - 2 v η)` on `2 v η < 1`: the variance of the member of natural parameter `η`. For
`v = 0`, both sides vanish. -/
@[simp]
theorem deriv_cgf_sub_sq_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (v : ℝ≥0) (hη : 2 * v * η < 1) :
    deriv (cgf (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) (gaussianReal m v)) η = v / (1 - 2 * v * η) := by
  rcases eq_or_ne v 0 with rfl | hv
  · -- Under the Dirac mass at `m`, the cumulant generating function of `(X - m) ^ 2` is zero.
    rw [show cgf (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) (gaussianReal m 0) = fun _ ↦ 0 from
      funext fun t ↦ by simp [cgf, gaussianReal_zero_var, mgf_dirac']]
    simp
  have hs : 0 < 1 - 2 * v * η := by linarith
  rw [← Measure.integral_expFamily ((mem_interior_integrableExpSet_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv).2 hη),
    expFamily_sub_sq_gaussianReal m v hη, integral_sub_sq_gaussianReal, sub_self,
    Real.coe_toNNReal _ (by positivity)]
  ring

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the squared deviation `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` is not almost everywhere constant under
`𝒩(m, v)`: it takes each value at most at two points, and the Gaussian law has no atoms. This is
the nondegeneracy assumption of the mean parametrization of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)`
with this statistic. -/
lemma not_ae_eq_const_sub_sq_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (c : ℝ) :
    ¬ (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) =ᵐ[gaussianReal m v] fun _ ↦ c := by
  have := nullSingletonClass_gaussianReal (μ := m) hv
  intro h
  obtain ⟨x, hx, hx₁, hx₂⟩ :=
    (h.and ((Measure.ae_ne _ (m + √c)).and (Measure.ae_ne _ (m - √c)))).exists
  have hx' : (x - m) ^ 2 = c := hx
  have hc : (x - m) ^ 2 = √c ^ 2 := by rw [sq_sqrt (hx' ▸ sq_nonneg _), hx']
  rcases sq_eq_sq_iff_eq_or_eq_neg.1 hc with h' | h'
  · exact hx₁ (by linarith)
  · exact hx₂ (by linarith)

/-- The value `(v⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2` of the natural parameter of the variance `μ`, written `η`,
satisfies `1 - 2 v η = v / μ`. -/
private lemma one_sub_two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv {v μ : ℝ} (hv : v ≠ 0) (hμ : μ ≠ 0) :
    1 - 2 * v * ((v⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2) = v / μ := by
  field_simp
  ring

/-- The value `(v⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2` of the natural parameter of a variance `μ > 0` is a natural
parameter: `2 v η < 1`. -/
private lemma two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv_lt_one (hv : v ≠ 0) (hμ : 0 < μ) :
    2 * v * (((v : ℝ)⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2) < 1 := by
  rw [← sub_pos, one_sub_two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv (NNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hv) hμ.ne']
  positivity

/-- The value `(v⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2` of the natural parameter of a variance `μ > 0` is mapped back to
`μ` by `η ↦ v / (1 - 2 v η)`. -/
private lemma div_one_sub_two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv {v μ : ℝ} (hv : v ≠ 0) (hμ : μ ≠ 0) :
    v / (1 - 2 * v * ((v⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2)) = μ := by
  rw [one_sub_two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv hv hμ, div_div_cancel₀ hv]

/-- The mean map of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` with statistic `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` maps the
value `(v⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2` back to the variance `μ > 0`. -/
private lemma deriv_cgf_sub_sq_gaussianReal_natParam (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (hμ : 0 < μ) :
    deriv (cgf (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) (gaussianReal m v)) (((v : ℝ)⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2) = μ := by
  rw [deriv_cgf_sub_sq_gaussianReal m v (two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv_lt_one hv hμ),
    div_one_sub_two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv (NNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hv) hμ.ne']

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the means of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` with statistic
`x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` are the variances `(0, ∞)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamilyMeans_sub_sq_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyMeans (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) = Ioi 0 := by
  ext μ
  rw [Measure.mem_expFamilyMeans_iff, mem_Ioi]
  refine ⟨fun ⟨η, hη, h⟩ ↦ ?_, fun hμ ↦ ⟨((v : ℝ)⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2,
    (mem_interior_integrableExpSet_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv).2
      (two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv_lt_one hv hμ), ?_⟩⟩
  · rw [mem_interior_integrableExpSet_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv] at hη
    have : 0 < 1 - 2 * v * η := by linarith
    rw [← h, deriv_cgf_sub_sq_gaussianReal m v hη]
    positivity
  · exact deriv_cgf_sub_sq_gaussianReal_natParam m hv hμ

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the natural parameter of the member of mean `μ > 0` (the variance) of the
exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` with statistic `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` is `(v⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2`. -/
@[simp]
theorem natParam_sub_sq_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (hμ : 0 < μ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).natParam (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) μ = ((v : ℝ)⁻¹ - μ⁻¹) / 2 := by
  have h := two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv_lt_one hv hμ
  have h_deriv := deriv_cgf_sub_sq_gaussianReal_natParam m hv hμ
  rw [← h_deriv, Measure.natParam_deriv_cgf (not_ae_eq_const_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv)
    ((mem_interior_integrableExpSet_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv).2 h), h_deriv]

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the member of mean `μ > 0` of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` with statistic
`x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` is `𝒩(m, μ)`. -/
theorem expFamily_natParam_sub_sq_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (hμ : 0 < μ) :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamily (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2)
      ((gaussianReal m v).natParam (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) μ) = gaussianReal m μ.toNNReal := by
  rw [natParam_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv hμ,
    expFamily_sub_sq_gaussianReal m v (two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv_lt_one hv hμ),
    div_one_sub_two_mul_mul_inv_sub_inv (NNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hv) hμ.ne']

/-- For `v ≠ 0`, the divergence of the exponential family of `𝒩(m, v)` with statistic
`x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` in the mean parametrization is `d(μ, μ') = (μ / μ' - 1 - log (μ / μ')) / 2` for
variances `μ, μ' > 0`, the relative entropy between `𝒩(m, μ)` and `𝒩(m, μ')`. It is the divergence
of the gamma laws of shape `1 / 2` (`expFamilyDiv_gammaMeasure`): `𝒩(m, v)` is a member of the
family of `𝒩(m, 1)`, which has the divergence of the natural exponential family of the law of
`(X - m) ^ 2` (`gaussianReal_map_sub_sq`). -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamilyDiv_sub_sq_gaussianReal (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (hμ : 0 < μ) (hμ' : 0 < μ') :
    (gaussianReal m v).expFamilyDiv (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) μ μ' =
      (μ / μ' - 1 - log (μ / μ')) / 2 := by
  have hv' : 0 < (v : ℝ) := NNReal.coe_pos.2 (pos_iff_ne_zero.2 hv)
  have h_means {x : ℝ} (hx : 0 < x) :
      x ∈ (gaussianReal m 1).expFamilyMeans (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) := by
    rwa [expFamilyMeans_sub_sq_gaussianReal m one_ne_zero]
  -- `𝒩(m, v)` is the member of mean `v` of the family of `𝒩(m, 1)`.
  rw [← Real.toNNReal_coe (r := v), ← expFamily_natParam_sub_sq_gaussianReal m one_ne_zero hv',
    Measure.expFamilyDiv_expFamily (not_ae_eq_const_sub_sq_gaussianReal m one_ne_zero)
      (interior_subset (Measure.natParam_mem_interior_integrableExpSet (h_means hv')))
      (h_means hμ) (h_means hμ'),
    ← Measure.expFamilyDiv_id_map (by fun_prop), gaussianReal_map_sub_sq,
    expFamilyDiv_gammaMeasure (by norm_num) (by norm_num) hμ hμ']
  ring

/-- For `v ≠ 0` and a variance `μ > 0`, the divergence `d(μ, μ')` of the exponential family of
`𝒩(m, v)` with statistic `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` tends to infinity as `μ'` tends to the endpoint `0` of
the means: it is the divergence of the gamma laws of shape `1 / 2`. -/
theorem tendsto_expFamilyDiv_sub_sq_gaussianReal_nhdsGT_zero (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (hμ : 0 < μ) :
    Filter.Tendsto ((gaussianReal m v).expFamilyDiv (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) μ) (𝓝[>] 0)
      Filter.atTop := by
  refine (tendsto_expFamilyDiv_gammaMeasure_nhdsGT_zero (a := 1 / 2) (r := 1 / 2) (by norm_num)
    (by norm_num) hμ).congr' ?_
  filter_upwards [self_mem_nhdsWithin] with μ' (hμ' : 0 < μ')
  rw [expFamilyDiv_gammaMeasure (by norm_num) (by norm_num) hμ hμ',
    expFamilyDiv_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv hμ hμ']
  ring

/-- For `v ≠ 0` and a variance `μ > 0`, the divergence `d(μ, μ')` of the exponential family of
`𝒩(m, v)` with statistic `x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2` tends to infinity as `μ'` tends to the endpoint `∞` of
the means. -/
theorem tendsto_expFamilyDiv_sub_sq_gaussianReal_atTop (m : ℝ) (hv : v ≠ 0) (hμ : 0 < μ) :
    Filter.Tendsto ((gaussianReal m v).expFamilyDiv (fun x ↦ (x - m) ^ 2) μ) Filter.atTop
      Filter.atTop := by
  refine (tendsto_expFamilyDiv_gammaMeasure_atTop (a := 1 / 2) (r := 1 / 2) (by norm_num)
    (by norm_num) hμ).congr' ?_
  filter_upwards [Filter.eventually_gt_atTop 0] with μ' hμ'
  rw [expFamilyDiv_gammaMeasure (by norm_num) (by norm_num) hμ hμ',
    expFamilyDiv_sub_sq_gaussianReal m hv hμ hμ']
  ring

end SubSq

end LMLExplore
